        <body>
            <div xml:id="d319">

                <pb facs="0657" n="547" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg547"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Porter to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1890-06-11"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 11, 1890</date>. (Received June
                        24.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 93.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 55, dated the 3d ultimo,
                    relating to the case of Nicolino Mileo, was duly received.</p>
                <p>I have not yet submitted the case to the minister for foreign affairs, having had
                    a desire, before doing so, to give a more careful study to the questions which
                    it involves.</p>
                <p>I expect to present Mileo’s case the first of next week, when the minister will
                    receive the members of the diplomatic corps. I shall first submit a note and
                    shall then ask that a special audience shall as soon afterwards as practicable
                    be given to me with regard to the case and with a view, also, of urging the
                    adoption of amendments to our treaties with Italy in relation to the subjects of
                    naturalization and the extradition of offenders.</p>
                <p>I have, etc,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. G. Porter.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
